     "Relations: how two factions treat each other. Relation is \"ally\", \"enemy\" or \"neutral\", and two factions without an entry are enemies. No factions are allies by default. Allies never fight and come to help each other; neutral factions leave each other's NPCs alone.",
     "ShareFriends (allies only): true makes each faction's members safe from the other's NPCs too, and lets them hire the other's NPCs. Otherwise a player is safe only from their own factions and hires only from them.",
     "MonsterCodes: creatures every faction attacks on sight (* is a wildcard). GrudgeSeconds: how long NPCs fight someone who hurt them or an ally. CallForHelpRange: how many blocks away allies come to help.",
-    "MaxAttackersPerTarget: how many NPCs may fight one NPC at a time. 0 (the default) means no limit. With a limit, the rest look for another enemy, wait one step behind in a battle line, or, outside a line, join a full enemy anyway when there is no other within reach. Either way an NPC takes an enemy nobody is fighting before one already being fought. Players are never limited, and an NPC always strikes back at whoever hits it.",
+    "RosterPerCaptain: one captain per this many places of a faction's roster (8 by default: Men 2, orcs and goblins 3, elves and dwarves 1, Uruk-hai and Dunlendings 2). Hiring or promoting past it is refused; captains a player already has stay. With several factions on one roster each captain counts its share. 0 means no limit.",
+    "MaxAttackersPerTarget: how many NPCs may fight one NPC at a time. 4 by default; 0 means no limit. With a limit, the rest look for another enemy, wait one step behind in a battle line, or, outside a line, join a full enemy anyway when there is no other within reach. Either way an NPC takes an enemy nobody is fighting before one already being fought. Players are never limited, and an NPC always strikes back at whoever hits it.",
     "CombatSpacing: how far apart, in blocks, fighting NPCs of the same side keep from each other, and the gap between neighbours in a battle line (0.8 to 4, 1.5 by default). Enemies only keep DuelDistanceMin apart. As many attackers as fit round an enemy this far apart (5 by default) fight it; the others take another enemy with room first, or else wait in a second ring one CombatSpacing farther out and step in when a place opens.",
     "DuelDistanceMin and DuelDistanceMax: how far from the center of the NPC it fights an attacker stands (1.0 to 1.6 blocks by default): it closes in when farther, steps back when closer, and stands and fights in between. Players are approached the vanilla way.",
-    "BattleLines (false by default: NPCs fight first and keep formation second): true makes groups of NPCs line up when they meet another faction's NPCs, waiting in their places until an enemy comes near: wild NPCs, and recruits following in any formation but Loose. Each NPC takes an enemy nobody is fighting first, so the lines pair off, and the extras join in on enemies already being fought (with a MaxAttackersPerTarget limit, the rest wait one step behind until a place opens). Wild NPCs and aggressive or raid recruits march to meet the enemy; defensive recruits hold their line until an enemy is within LineHoldRange blocks. Loose followers, guards, archers, and fights with players or monsters don't make lines.",
+    "BattleLines (true by default): groups of NPCs line up when they meet another faction's NPCs, waiting in their places until an enemy comes near: wild NPCs, and recruits following in any formation but Loose. The front rank has one place per enemy; when the lines meet each front NPC fights the enemy facing it from its place in the line. NPCs past that (the side outnumbers the enemy) wait one step behind until the lines meet, then go round to surround, up to MaxAttackersPerTarget on one enemy. Wild NPCs and aggressive or raid recruits march to meet the enemy; defensive recruits hold their line until an enemy is within LineHoldRange blocks. Loose followers, guards, archers, and fights with players or monsters don't make lines. false lets NPCs fight as they find enemies.",
     "HelmetChance: the chance (0 to 1) that a newly spawned NPC that may go bare-headed wears its outfit's helmet. Which units may go bare-headed is set by the mod for each unit (all orcs and Uruk-hai, and the units of other factions marked so); the others always spawn with theirs. A helmet it doesn't wear is kept, and its owner can put it on or take any helmet off from the recruit's menu. Helmets are only for looks: NPC protection comes from rank. CaptainsAlwaysHelmeted: true makes every captain always wear theirs (false by default since 0.0.82).",
     "ShieldChance: the chance (0 to 1) that a newly spawned Mordor orc carries a shield. Shields are only for looks, are never carried with the poleaxe, and the owner can take one off or put it on from the recruit's menu.",
